---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { app } from '../config';
---
<Layout title="Ancrate support — Setup, shortcuts & troubleshooting" description="Get help connecting Apple Notes, collecting tasks, using slash commands, setting up widgets and MCP, or contacting Ancrate support.">
  <div class="document wrap">
    <header class="document-header"><p class="eyebrow">Here to help</p><h1>Make yourself<br />at home.</h1><p>Set up Ancrate, find your next steps, and get back to your notes.</p><a class="button primary" href={`mailto:${app.supportEmail}?subject=Ancrate%20support`}>Email support <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small-note"><a href={`mailto:${app.supportEmail}`}>{app.supportEmail}</a></p></header>
    <div class="document-grid"><aside><nav aria-label="Support topics"><a href="#get-started">Get started</a><a href="#sources">Choose your to-dos</a><a href="#task-panel">The task panel</a><a href="#slash-commands">Slash commands</a><a href="#widgets">Desktop widgets</a><a href="#mcp">MCP setup</a><a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav></aside><div class="prose">
      <section id="get-started"><h2>Connect your library.</h2><p>Ancrate requires macOS 14 or later. Open the app and choose <strong>Choose Notes Folder</strong>, or go to <strong>Settings → Library</strong>. Confirm the <code>group.com.apple.notes</code> folder shown in the system picker.</p><p>Click <strong>Check Again</strong> if access is unavailable. If macOS still blocks the selected store, follow the app’s Full Disk Access fallback guidance. Accessibility permission is separate and is only needed for optional Notes shortcuts.</p><p>Prefer to look around first? Choose <strong>Explore with sample notes</strong>. Sample notes are not shared with widgets or MCP clients.</p></section>
      <section id="sources"><h2>Choose what counts.</h2><p>Use <strong>All to-dos</strong>, <strong>Past month</strong>, or <strong>Past 3 months</strong>. Recent ranges follow the source note’s date, rather than the date of an individual task. You can choose last-edited or creation date in Settings.</p><p>In <strong>Settings → To-do sources</strong>, include the folders you want. Right-click a note or task to exclude its source note; restore it from the note’s menu or the sources settings. Your notes remain in your library.</p><p>These choices affect the to-do lists and widget snapshot. <strong>They do not restrict MCP access to the library.</strong></p></section>
      <section id="task-panel"><h2>Keep your tasks nearby.</h2><p>Choose <strong>Show To-dos</strong> from Ancrate’s menu-bar icon. Search by task, note title, or folder. Click a task, or select it and press Return, to open its source in Apple Notes.</p><p><strong>Change task completion in the original note.</strong> Ancrate reflects those changes when it refreshes. Pin the panel if you want it to stay beside your work.</p><p>The default Notes-only shortcut is <kbd>⌃⌥T</kbd>. You can change or disable it in Settings. It requires Accessibility permission.</p></section>
      <section id="slash-commands"><h2>A quicker start in Notes.</h2><ol><li>Enable slash commands in Ancrate’s Settings.</li><li>Allow Ancrate in <strong>System Settings → Privacy & Security → Accessibility</strong>, then click <strong>Check Again</strong> in Ancrate.</li><li>Keep Ancrate running and open an editable, unlocked note in Apple Notes.</li><li>Type <kbd>/</kbd> at the start of a line. Choose with ↑ and ↓, then apply with Return or Tab. Escape dismisses the menu.</li></ol><p>Commands include headings, lists, checklists, quotes, and tables. <code>/todo</code> creates a checklist. <code>/tasks</code>, <code>/month</code>, and <code>/quarter</code> open your collected to-do lists.</p><p>Try commands in a temporary note first. Accepted commands remove the typed token and use Notes’ native editing and formatting actions. Use Notes’ Undo if needed. Notes updates or custom formatting shortcuts can affect compatibility.</p></section>
      <section id="widgets"><h2>Give your desktop a next step.</h2><p>Right-click the desktop and choose <strong>Edit Widgets → Ancrate</strong>. Add a small, medium, or large widget, then edit it to choose its time range.</p><p>Widgets show the last local snapshot and may keep showing it while Ancrate is closed. Keep the app running for fresh updates; macOS controls when widgets redraw. Ancrate refreshes its library every minute while running. Use <strong>Refresh</strong> or <kbd>⌘R</kbd> to check sooner.</p><p>Turn off <strong>Show my to-dos in the Ancrate widget</strong> in Settings to replace the stored tasks with an empty snapshot. macOS controls when that change appears in the visible widget.</p><p>Enable <strong>Launch at Login</strong> in <strong>Settings → Application</strong> if you want Ancrate ready after signing in. Closing the window leaves the menu-bar app running; <strong>Quit Ancrate</strong> stops it.</p></section>
      <section id="mcp"><h2>Connect your local AI client.</h2><p>Connect the Notes library first. In <strong>Settings → MCP setup</strong>, choose <strong>Copy configuration</strong> and add it to your client’s MCP configuration. Restart the client after changing folder access. If you move Ancrate, copy its configuration again.</p><p>Each client launches its own local server process; the main app can be closed. Four read-only tools are available: <code>list_notes</code>, <code>search_notes</code>, <code>get_note</code>, and <code>get_checklists</code>. MCP cannot edit notes.</p><p><strong>To-do filters do not limit MCP access.</strong> A connected client may send returned note content to its AI provider or other services. Review that client’s privacy settings before connecting private notes.</p></section>
      <section id="troubleshooting"><h2>Something not quite right?</h2>
        <details><summary>I can’t see my notes.</summary><p>Choose the Notes folder again in Settings → Library and check access. A saved selection may have expired. If macOS still blocks the store, follow the in-app Full Disk Access fallback. Locked notes may not expose their content.</p></details>
        <details><summary>My to-do list is empty or missing a task.</summary><p>Check the date range, open/completed filter, included folders, and excluded notes. Recent ranges use the note’s date. Change completion in the original Apple Note, then refresh Ancrate.</p></details>
        <details><summary>The slash menu doesn’t appear.</summary><p>Keep Ancrate running, enable slash commands, confirm Accessibility permission, and click Check Again. Type / on a new line in an editable, unlocked Apple Note. Notes updates and custom formatting shortcuts may affect compatibility.</p></details>
        <details><summary>My widget hasn’t updated.</summary><p>Confirm widget sharing is enabled, keep Ancrate running, and refresh the library. Widgets display a local snapshot. macOS controls redraw timing, so an update may not appear immediately.</p></details>
        <details><summary>I closed the window. How do I open Ancrate?</summary><p>Use the menu-bar icon → Open Ancrate. Ancrate hides its Dock icon by default. Dock visibility and Launch at Login are optional in Settings.</p></details>
        <details><summary>My MCP client can’t connect.</summary><p>Connect the real Notes library, copy a fresh configuration from Settings → MCP setup, and restart your client. Copy the configuration again after moving the app. Sample notes are not available through MCP.</p></details>
      </section>
      <section id="contact"><h2>Let’s work it out.</h2><p>For questions, bug reports, or feedback, email <a href={`mailto:${app.supportEmail}?subject=Ancrate%20support`}>{app.supportEmail}</a>.</p><p>Include what you expected, what happened, and the app and macOS versions. <strong>Help & Setup → Copy support info</strong> copies only the app/build and macOS versions, without note content, titles, or folder paths. Use a sample note if you attach a screenshot.</p><p>For questions about your data, see the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> or contact the same address.</p></section>
    </div></div>
  </div>
</Layout>
